3: Ib. X. ५२. (५६. V. १२).
went from Balabhadra and learnt गदा from बलराम at मिथिला;
4: Ib. X. ५७. २६; Br. III. ७१. ८४; वा. ९६. ८३.
mistook the colour of the flooring of the पाण्डव's सभा (built by Maya) for a sheet of water and had a nasty fall at which भीम and the ladies laughed. This enraged Duryodhana who was conciliated by युधिष्ठिर who sent clothes to him through कृष्ण. He did not accept them, but went home downcast;
5: भा. X. ५८. २७; ७५. ३४-39.
kept under influence Vinda and Anuvinda of Avanti;
6: Ib. X. ५८. ३०.
banished the पाण्डवस् and द्रौपदी to the forest for defeat in the game of dice;
7: Ib. X. ६४. [4].
resented साम्ब's action in taking away his daughter लक्ष्मणा in स्वयम्वर and wanted to punish him; heard of राम's arrival and extended welcome to him; afraid of राम's prowess agreed to the marriage of his daughter to साम्ब and gave a rich dowry;
8: Ib. X. ६८. (whole); Vi. V. ३

